  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $a=8i-2j+4k$ and $b=6i+4j-\\frac{1}{2}k.$ Find $a\\times b.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 8 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1-16)i-(-4-24)j+(32+12)k \\\\  & =-15i+28j+44k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
